            <ArticleTitle>A serious pain in the neck.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of internal carotid artery dissection, an important cause of ischemic cerebrovascular disease. Presentations include a headache, which is usually unilateral to the side of carotid dissection, sharp, nonthrobbing in nature with radiation from the neck. The clinical presentations, investigations, and treatment of the disease are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
